## 3. mapZoomReach.test.tsx — one cohort case for `isDiveTarget`

`isDiveTarget` now reads `focus.isStructuralKind` instead of a third copy of
`root|track|entity`, so a cohort is a world you fly INTO rather than a leaf that
opens the sidebar. That is a behaviour change with no assertion in the suite that
owns the function's tests:

```ts
it('dives into a cohort rather than opening the org sidebar on it', () => {
  const cohort = { ...node, kind: 'cohort', bucketKey: cohortKeyOf('manager', 'sara'),
                   children: [orgNode] }
  expect(isDiveTarget(cohort)).toBe(true)
})
```

The failure it guards is specific: with the old comparison a cohort answered
`false`, so Enter on the biggest ring on the screen called `dive.details(id)` and
handed a synthetic key to the organization panel.

