## 4. model.ts — one sentence in `KIND_ROLE`'s doc is now inaccurate

> `worlds.ts`' STRUCTURAL_KINDS and `focus.ts`' `isPlaceKind` are this row.

The first half is exactly right and this unit made it true (`STRUCTURAL_KINDS`
gained `'cohort'`; `focus.isStructuralKind` is now literally
`KIND_ROLE[kind] === 'place'`). The second half is not: `focus.isPlaceKind` is
`canFocus`'s narrower exception — "does framing this node still answer something
when it holds nothing" — which is `entity` and `cohort` and deliberately NOT
`root` or `track`. focus.ts's header argues the exclusion at length (an empty
track is drawn so that "which track has nothing on it" is visible, which is a
different claim from "make it the screen"). Suggested: replace `isPlaceKind`
with `focus.ts`' `isStructuralKind` in that sentence.

